(1)

where α, β and γ are constants, and Cµνρσ is the Weyl tensor. Notice that for any static, spherically
symmetric black-hole solution, the term quadratic in Ricci scalar R makes no contribution to the
corresponding field equations [6]. As a result, this setting of β = 0 and γ = 1 has been often
applied for simplicity in the Einstein-Weyl (EW) gravity, and this theory reduces to the pure
Einstein-Weyl gravity. By fixed α = 1/2, Lü et.al [4, 5] derived a new numerical non-Schwarzschild
∗

